{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PTEC Unit Vent Controller - Application 6677 (Heating and DX Cooling, ASHRAE Cycles I and II)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6677-unit-ventilator-dx-ashrae-cycles-i-ii",
  "short_model": "PTEC Unit Ventilator DX 6677",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6677",
    "Application 6677",
    "App 6677",
    "550-493PA",
    "Siemens unit ventilator DX",
    "ASHRAE Cycle II"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Unit ventilator (terminal unit) controller",
  "applies_to": "Unit ventilators with a DX cooling coil and/or a hot water, steam or electric heating coil, run to ASHRAE Cycles I and II on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit vent controller 550-493PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6677 controls a unit ventilator with DX cooling to ASHRAE Cycles I and II on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP. In heating a room loop resets the discharge air setpoint (DISCH STPT between DSH MIN TEMP and DSH MAX TEMP) and the heating valve, face-bypass damper or electric stages hold it; in cooling the DX stage cycles with minimum on/off times. It also drives the outdoor air damper, auxiliary radiation, morning warm-up/cool-down, night override and free cooling.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F, Btu/lb); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "LOW TEMP DET (BI 26) state texts are printed as Active = OFF and Inactive = ON; they are kept as printed.",
    "Cooling-only units are run by holding HEAT.COOL at COOL."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Vent - Heating and DX Cooling, ASHRAE Cycles I and II, Application 6677, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1182",
    "revision_date": "2018-01-23",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/MFVQZau2lm3VGnPJvGYXgQ/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the unit to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, turns free cooling on and off with FREE CLG (BO 23), and reads room temperature, fan and DX status, discharge air temperature, outdoor air damper position, the low temperature detector and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 23",
        "name": "FREE CLG",
        "why": "Free cooling / economizer enable"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 50",
        "name": "FAN",
        "why": "Fan on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 44",
        "name": "DX",
        "why": "DX cooling on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 26",
        "name": "LOW TEMP DET",
        "why": "Low temperature detection thermostat"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "The field panel (or PPCL) turns the free cooling/economizer function on and off by writing FREE CLG (BO 23).",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6695."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "As shipped, the controller keeps all equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, biases, output span/start settings and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
      "A low temperature detection thermostat on BI 26 is strongly recommended for hot water and steam coils.",
      "If the discharge air sensor fails, heat goes off and the outdoor air damper closes (or the unit shuts down); temperature control stops until it returns."
    ]
  },
